When `adf_dev_up()` partially completes and fails, it may have already registered IRQ handlers via `adf_isr_resource_alloc()`. However, the failure path in `adf_probe()` does not call `adf_dev_down()` to detach those handlers. Subsequently, when devres runs `pcim_msi_release()` (registered by `pci_alloc_irq_vectors()` inside `adf_dev_up()` or earlier), the MSI-X vectors are freed while the IRQ handlers are still attached, causing `remove_proc_entry()` warnings.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
<text>
if (ret) {
