    return ret;
}
</text>
Reason:
By explicitly calling `adf_dev_down()` when `adf_dev_up()` fails, the IRQ handlers are properly detached before returning. This ensures that when devres later releases the MSI-X vectors (via `pcim_msi_release()`), no handlers remain attached, preventing the `remove_proc_entry()` warning and ensuring correct cleanup order.

